# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lead delivery — REQUIRED
#
# Without this the contact form and the chat widget both return a visible
# error rather than accepting a lead. That is deliberate: an unconfigured
# deploy should fail loudly, not swallow enquiries while showing
# "Message received."
#
# Get the access key from https://web3forms.com — it is tied to the address
# leads are delivered to.
#
# NOTE: this is NEXT_PUBLIC_, so it is compiled into the JavaScript bundle and
# is visible in page source. That is Web3Forms' intended model (it is an
# *access key*, not a secret), and it is browser-side because their free plan
# refuses server-side submissions: "Use our API in client side ... Pro plan is
# required."
#
# Because it is public, two things are not optional:
#   1. Web3Forms dashboard → Settings → Domain Restriction → andrethomaslaw.com
#   2. Leave their spam filtering enabled
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=
